<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Data Bridge: Queue Processor could not be started</title>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <style type="text/css">
        body {
            font-family: Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif;
            font-size: 14px;
        }

        .button {
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            border: none;
            color: white;
            padding: 15px 32px;
            text-align: center;
            text-decoration: none;
            display: inline-block;
            font-size: 16px;
            margin: 1em 0;
        }

        dt {
            font-weight: bold;
            text-decoration: underline;
            margin-top: 1.5em;
        }

        dd {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0 0 0.5em 0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<p>When Data Bridge jobs get queued, queue processing will be started automatically. In this case this did not work. You can start queue processing manually with the following button.</p>
<a href="{{ startQueueProcessorUrl }}" class="button">Start queue processing</a>
<p>If you receive mails like this frequently, something is not configured correctly, which prevents automatic start of the queue processing. Potential causes can be:
<dl>
    <dt>Different PHP version used by webserver and command line interface (CLI)</dt>
    <dd>Ensure that <code>php -v</code> returns the same version as used by your webserver (Apache / Nginx). Check <code>which php</code> to look up to which PHP binary the <code>php</code> command refers to.</dd>
    <dd>If you cannot link the correct PHP binary (e.g. because of multi-site setup with different PHP versions), add <code>opendxp_executable_php: /usr/local/custom-php/bin/php</code> (in section <code>parameters</code> to your <code>{{ configFilePath }}</code></dd>

    <dt>Missing write permission to OpenDXP's temporary folder <code>{{ opendxpRootFolder }}/var/tmp</code></dt>
    <dd>Set up folder to be writable by webserver user, e.g. with <code>chmod -R u+w {{ opendxpRootFolder }}/var/</code> (as everything inside OpenDXP's var folder should be writable). Please also assure that the folder belongs to user <code>{{ webserverUser }}</code>.</dd>

    <dt>Error in queued job</dt>
    <dd>The queued job which could not be executed is <code>{{ queueItem.command }} -vv</code>. Please try to execute this manually on the command line. If this job fails, it will never get removed from the queue. If it succeeds, the problem is something else.</dd>
</dl>
</body>
</html>